{"t": 1795060504.06588, "kind": "assistant", "text": "## Stopped before production: PHP 8.3 checks failed\n\n- Created dev snapshot: `dev/Pre-PHP-8.3-security-upgrade.tgz`\n- Upgraded **dev only** from PHP 8.1.34 to **PHP 8.3.31**\n- Both required pages now fail on dev:\n  - `/` → **500**, PHP fatal error\n  - `/?p=1` → **500**, PHP fatal error\n- Both errors name the active security plugin **`limit-login-attempts-reloaded` 3.4.4**\n\nI did **not** deactivate the security plugin or make any production changes. Production remains on PHP 8.1.34, and I have not submitted a production upgrade plan because the dev validation failed. The plugin’s PHP 8.3 compatibility must be resolved and both pages retested successfully before production can be considered."}
{"t": 1795060504.066234, "kind": "stop", "reason": "end_turn"}
